  "reasoning": "The facts describe three distinct criminal conduct: (1) the official accepted cash, shopping cards and gold in exchange for using his position – this is bribery (受贿). (2) He diverted public funds from a state‑owned enterprise to a private individual without proper authorization – this is embezzlement of public funds (挪用公款). (3) A large portion of his personal wealth cannot be accounted for by lawful income, indicating concealment of illicit proceeds – this matches the crime of concealing/obscuring criminal proceeds (掩饰、隐瞒犯罪所得、犯罪所得收益). Therefore the appropriate charges are the three listed crimes.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]受贿;挪用公款;掩饰、隐瞒犯罪所得、犯罪所得收益<eoa>"
